Update the existing Document Checklist to show a warning when the user tries to close it with unsaved changes.

If the user makes any changes in the Document Checklist and clicks the X/Close button without saving, display:

"Document Checklist is not saved. Continue ?"

The user should get Yes and No options.

- Yes → Close the Document Checklist and discard the unsaved changes.
- No → Keep the Document Checklist open with the current changes.

If there are no unsaved changes, the Document Checklist should close normally without showing the warning.

After the user successfully saves the changes, closing the Document Checklist should also happen normally without showing the warning.

Use the existing project implementation and confirmation mechanism with the minimum required change.
